---
import fs from 'node:fs';
import path from 'node:path';
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { Header, Footer } from '../components/ui';
import '../styles/business.css';
type Credit = { text: string; author: string; title: string; sourcePage: string; sourceRevision: string; license: string; licenseUrl: string; changes: string; sourceProject: string; copyrightNotice?: string; additionalAttribution?: string; originalLicenseNotice?: string };
const frenchCredits: Credit[] = JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(path.resolve(process.cwd(), '../audio/human-pilot/attribution.json'), 'utf8')).records;
const englishCredits: Credit[] = ['human-en-i-ih', 'human-en-ae-strut'].flatMap(folder => JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(path.resolve(process.cwd(), `public/audio/${folder}/attribution.json`), 'utf8')).records);
const germanCredits: Credit[] = JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(path.resolve(process.cwd(), 'public/audio/human-de-i-length/attribution.json'), 'utf8')).records;
---
<Base title="Audio credits | MinimalPairs" description="Recording sources, contributors and licenses." noindex>
  <Header /><main class="editorial-wrap"><p class="eyebrow">THE VOICES YOU HEAR</p><h1>Audio credits.</h1><p class="editorial-lede">Recording sources, contributors and licenses.</p>
    
    <section id="french-recordings"><h2>French · Sartus85 and Poslovitch</h2><div class="editorial-panel"><strong>Reuse and changes</strong><p>Sartus85’s six MP3s are provided under <a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/">CC BY-SA 4.0</a>. Poslovitch’s six recordings remain under <a href="https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/">CC0 1.0</a>. Each original WAV was converted to 192 kbps MP3, with its sample rate and channel count preserved and file metadata removed. We made no edits to timing, pitch, speed, loudness or spoken content.</p><p>The licenses apply to the individual recordings listed below. Crediting these speakers does not imply their endorsement of MinimalPairs.</p></div><div class="credit-list">{frenchCredits.map(credit => <article><h3>{credit.text} <span>· {credit.author}</span></h3><p><a href={credit.sourcePage}>{credit.title}</a><br />{credit.sourceProject} · <a href={credit.licenseUrl}>{credit.license}</a> · <a href={credit.sourceRevision}>Audited source revision</a></p><details><summary>Recording changes</summary><p>{credit.changes}</p></details></article>)}</div></section>
    <section id="english-recordings"><h2>English · Grendelkhan and Dvortygirl</h2><div class="editorial-panel"><strong>Reuse and changes</strong><p>Grendelkhan’s twelve recordings are provided under <a href="https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/">CC0 1.0</a>. Dvortygirl’s twelve recordings are provided under the <a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0/">CC BY-SA 3.0</a> option offered by their source pages. These licenses remain separate and apply to the individual recordings.</p><p>The original WAV or Ogg files were converted to 192 kbps, 44.1 kHz mono MP3. Sample-rate conversion and stereo downmix were applied where needed; metadata was removed. There was no trimming, denoising, time stretching, pitch shifting or loudness normalization. Downmix may affect channel balance. Exact changes and original notices are retained per recording.</p><p>The source identifies one profile as US English, and both contributors publicly declare native English. Their actual accent and suitability for this exercise have not been independently listening-verified.</p></div><div class="credit-list">{englishCredits.map(credit => <article><h3>{credit.text} <span>· {credit.author}</span></h3><p><a href={credit.sourcePage}>{credit.title}</a><br />{credit.sourceProject} · <a href={credit.licenseUrl}>{credit.license}</a> · <a href={credit.sourceRevision}>Audited source revision</a></p>{credit.additionalAttribution && <p>Additional source credit: {credit.additionalAttribution}</p>}{credit.copyrightNotice && <p>Original copyright notice: {credit.copyrightNotice}</p>}{credit.originalLicenseNotice && <p>Original embedded notice: “{credit.originalLicenseNotice}”. The distribution license selected from the source page is {credit.license}.</p>}<details><summary>Recording changes</summary><p>{credit.changes}</p></details></article>)}</div></section>
    <section id="german-recordings"><h2>German · Jeuwre and joni</h2><div class="editorial-panel"><strong>Two-pair listening preview</strong><p>This small collection contains only <em>in / ihn</em> and <em>im / ihm</em>: four words recorded by each contributor. Jeuwre’s four recordings retain <a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/">CC BY-SA 4.0</a>. Joni’s four retain the <a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0/">CC BY-SA 3.0</a> option established by their source pages’ license migration. Each file keeps its own license and attribution.</p><p>The source identifies Jeuwre as a native German speaker from Berlin. Joni’s native-language and regional background are unestablished. These source credits do not independently verify audible speaker identity, accent or pronunciation.</p><p>Both contributors’ source-file version dates correlate with the target vowel category. That metadata pattern is not proof of an audible cue, but the recordings are not a controlled same-session collection and need listening review. With only four words, repeated practice can also become token memorization; this preview does not measure transfer to unfamiliar words or speakers.</p><p>The original Ogg/Vorbis files were converted to mono 44.1 kHz, 192 kbps MP3. No trimming, denoising, pitch shifting, time stretching or loudness normalization was applied. Full per-file changes are below. <a href="/audio/human-de-i-length/attribution.json">Download the attribution record.</a></p></div><div class="credit-list">{germanCredits.map(credit => <article><h3>{credit.text} <span>· {credit.author}</span></h3><p><a href={credit.sourcePage}>{credit.title}</a><br />{credit.sourceProject} · <a href={credit.licenseUrl}>{credit.license}</a> · <a href={credit.sourceRevision}>Audited source revision</a></p>{credit.additionalAttribution && <p>Additional source credit: {credit.additionalAttribution}</p>}{credit.copyrightNotice && <p>Original copyright notice: {credit.copyrightNotice}</p>}{credit.originalLicenseNotice && <p>Original embedded notice: “{credit.originalLicenseNotice}”. The distribution license selected from the source page is {credit.license}.</p>}<details><summary>Recording changes</summary><p>{credit.changes}</p></details></article>)}</div></section>
    
    
    
  </main><Footer />
</Base>
<style>.credit-list{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:16px}.credit-list article{border:1px solid #dce3d7;background:#fff;border-radius:12px;padding:22px;min-width:0}.credit-list h3{font-size:20px;font-weight:600;margin:0 0 9px}.credit-list h3 span{font-size:14px;font-weight:400;color:#566159}.credit-list p{margin:8px 0 0;font-size:13px;overflow-wrap:anywhere}.credit-list details{font-size:12px;margin-top:13px}.credits-actions{display:flex;align-items:center;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:20px}@media(max-width:600px){.credit-list{grid-template-columns:1fr}}</style>
